        heals-ing:CuminPowder,
        heals-ing:Curd,
        heals-ing:MintLeaves,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:Salt ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Beetroot Carrot Raita Recipe, grate the carrots and beetroots and set aside.Meanwhile, whisk yogurt in a bowl, add roasted cumin powder, red chilli powder, chaat masala and salt to taste.Now add grated carrot and beetroot.
Mix everything well and garnish it with mint leaves.
Serve cold.Serve Beetroot Carrot Raita Recipe along with Peshawari Chole and Phulkas for a weekday lunch or dinner."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-carrot-raita-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 25 .

heals:BeetrootChickenCutletsRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Beetroot Chicken Cutlets Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Snack" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Indian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:NonVegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/roopakamath1997-gmail.com/BeetrootChicken_Cutlets___original1_edited.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Beetroot,
        heals-ing:BonelessChicken,
        heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:CuminSeeds,
        heals-ing:CurryLeaves,
        heals-ing:GaramMasalaPowder,
        heals-ing:GingerGarlicPaste,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:Potatoes,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil,
        heals-ing:WholeBlackPeppercorns,
        heals-ing:WholeWheatBreadCrumbs ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making Beetroot Chicken Cutlets Recipe, heat 3-4 cups water in a deep-bottomed saucepan, add salt and pepper and bring to boil.Add the chicken and cook it for about 20 minutes or till the chicken is cooked.Meanwhile, in a mixing bowl mash the potato until no lumps are present and grate the cooked beetroot into it.
Once chicken has cooked, drain the water and let cool.
Once cooled, shred the chicken.
Mix the shredded chicken, mashed potato, grated beetroot, green chillies, ginger-garlic paste, coriander leaves, and curry leaves, jeera, chilli powder and garam masala.Adjust the salt and mix until you get a smooth but firm dough like consistency.Make round cutlets by making medium sized balls, and press them between your palms, and coat it with bread crumbs.
Arrange on parchment paper until all the cutlets are made.
Drizzle oil in a shallow frying pan and place the cutlets on pan.
Take care to place the cutlets sparsely on the pan and not to overcrowd the pan, to help them shallow fry evenly.
You can shallow fry them in batches.Flip to the other side when the bottom of cutlets is nicely crisp and browning.Serve Beetroot Chicken Cutlets Recipe as party appetizers along with Dhaniya Pudina Chutney Recipe or Party Style Creamy Spinach Dip Made with Cheesy Garlic Mayo, may be along with Vegetarian Tandoori Kebab Recipe."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-chicken-cutlets-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 50 .

heals:BeetrootChutneyRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Beetroot Chutney Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Condiment" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:SouthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Pooja_Thakur/Beetroot_chutney.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Asafoetida,
        heals-ing:Beetroot,
        heals-ing:ChanaDal,
        heals-ing:CurryLeaves,
        heals-ing:FreshCoconut,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:MustardSeeds,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SesameOil,
        heals-ing:Water,
        heals-ing:WhiteUradDal ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Beetroot Chutney recipe, heat oil in pan.Add bengal gram and black gram, saute them till both lentils become golden in colour.
Make sure you don’t burn them.Now add asafoetida, curry leaves and saute it for a few seconds.Add grated beetroot and chopped green chillies.
Saute them for 5 to 6 minutes or till the raw aroma of beetroot goes away.Switch off the flame and add grated coconut, mix well.
Let the mixture bit cool down.Once the mixture is cooled down, add it to a grinder jar.
Add salt, some water and grind it in a smooth paste.Take the smooth paste in a bowl.
Now we will start making the tempering for chutney.Heat oil in a tadka pan.
Add mustard seeds and let them crackle.Now add curry leaves and pinch of asafoetida, mix well and switch off flame.
Pour the tempering over beetroot chutney mixture.
Mix well and Beetroot Chutney is ready to be served.Serve Beetroot Chutney along with Keerai Sambar and Steamed rice for a healthy and tasty weekday lunch or dinner."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-chutney-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 40 .

heals:BeetrootJuiceRecipeWithCucumberPineapple a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Beetroot Juice Recipe With Cucumber & Pineapple" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Beverage" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Continental ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/World_Beverages/Beetroot_Juice_Recipe_with_Cucumber_and_Pineapple-1.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Beetroot,
        heals-ing:Cucumber,
        heals-ing:Ginger,
        heals-ing:LemonJuice,
        heals-ing:Pineapple,
        heals-ing:Water ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Beetroot Juice With Cucumber & Pineapple Recipe add beetroot, cucumber, pineapple and ginger to a food processor or blender and make a fine puree.Pour the puree into a strainer and extract the juice completely.Add the pulp back to food processor or blender along with cold water and blend again.
Strain this second juice once again and add to the first extract.Stir both the extract together, add in the lemon juice and serve chilled.
Check the taste and adjust the sweetness by adding honey or more pineapple.
You can also optionally add salt if you like it salty.Serve this Beetroot Juice With Cucumber & Pineapple along with Grilled Hummus Paneer Bhurji Sandwich Recipe  for a healthy wholesome breakfast."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-juice-recipe-with-cucumber-and-pineapple"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 15 .

heals:BeetrootLoniSpongeDosaRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Beetroot Loni Sponge Dosa Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Breakfast" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:NorthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Megha_Joshi/How_to_make_Beetroot_Loni_Sponge_Dosa_with_Potato_PalyaBhaji_and_Coconut_Chutney.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Beetroot,
        heals-ing:Butter,
        heals-ing:Buttermilk,
        heals-ing:CookingSoda,
        heals-ing:CurryLeaves,
        heals-ing:GreenChilliPaste,
        heals-ing:IdliDosaBatter,
        heals-ing:Poha,
        heals-ing:Rice,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SesameOil ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Beetroot Loni Sponge Dosa recipe, wash rice 2 to 3 times and then along with Poha soak it for overnight in sour buttermilk.Next Morning, grind the soaked Rice and Poha into a smooth consistency batter in a mixer grinder.
Add salt giving it stir and keep it aside.In a mixer grinder, add the peeled beetroot, curry leaves and blend it without water into a paste.
Take a sieve and squeeze beet juice and add it to Sponge Dosa Batter.Add green chillies to the batter and mix the batter gently.Heat up a non-stick tawa and sprinkle water to check its temperature.
If there is a sizzle then its temperature is correct.Add cooking soda in the Dosa Batter and give it a quick whips in same direction.Pour in two ladles of batter on the tawa turning the flame to low.
Add oil across the edges and cover it with a lid.Take a Loni/Butter in your hand and drop it on sponge Dosa generously.
Let the butter smear on the Dosa.
Flip it on other side to get it more crusty.Serve Beetroot Loni Sponge Dosa with Mixed Vegetable Sambar and South Indian Coconut Chutney for a delicious and healthy breakfast."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-loni-sponge-dosa-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 40 .

heals:BeetrootMilletPaniyaramRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Beetroot Millet Paniyaram Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Breakfast",
        "Snack" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Chettinad ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Preeti_Tamilarasan/Beetroot_Millet_Paniyaram.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BakingPowder,
        heals-ing:Beetroot,
        heals-ing:CardamomPowder,
        heals-ing:FoxtailMillet,
        heals-ing:Ghee,
        heals-ing:InstantOats,
        heals-ing:Jaggery,
        heals-ing:RiceFlour ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Beetroot Millet Paniyaram Recipe, soak foxtail millet in warm water for 2-3 hours.
Once soaked well drain water completely and blend the millet in a mixer grinder to smooth batter without adding water.Add chopped beetroot to this and blend again.
Transfer the batter to a mixing bowl.Add oats, rice flour, baking powder, powdered jaggery and cardamom powder.
Mix everything well.
Add a little water to make a thick pouring batter.Heat Paniyaram pan on low-medium heat.
 Pour 1 teaspoon ghee into each cavity of the pan.
Spoon the Beetroot Millet Paniyaram batter into the cavities.
Don't fill it to the brim, but only 3/4th full.Cover the pan with a lid and cook on low to medium heat for about 3 to 4 minutes until the top of the paniyaram is steamed.
Once the top looks steamed, flip the Beetroot Paniyarams over the cook on the other side (without closing the lid) until golden brown.Once each Paniyaram is cooked, remove from the pan and pour another batch of batter and proceed the similar way.Serve this Beetroot Millet Paniyaram as a high protein snack for kids or as a dessert for parties."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/beetroot-millet-paniyaram-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 190 .

heals:BeetrootPaneerCurryRecipeInCoconutMilkBeetPaneerCurryRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
