heals:GramAndPotatoDryVegetableRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Gram and Potato Dry Vegetable Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Side Dish" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:NorthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Nithya_Anantham/Chana_Aur_Aloo_Ki_Sookhi_Subzi_Recipe.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Amchur,
        heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:CorianderPowder,
        heals-ing:CuminSeeds,
        heals-ing:GaramMasalaPowder,
        heals-ing:Ginger,
        heals-ing:GingerGarlicPaste,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:KabuliChana,
        heals-ing:Onion,
        heals-ing:Potatoes,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil,
        heals-ing:Tomatoes,
        heals-ing:TurmericPowder ;
    fkg:hasInstruction "To begin making Chana Aur Aloo Ki Sookhi Sabzi, soak the chickpea or chana over night and pressure cook the soaked chana in enough water for 3 whistles and keep aside.Similarly, wash and boil the potatoes with 1 cup water in a pressure cooker for 2 whistles; peal the skin, cut into cubes and keep aside.Heat oil in a pan on medium heat, add the cumin seeds and let it splutter.Add the finely chopped onions and saute until it turns transparent.Add the ginger and garlic paste and cook until the raw smell goes away.Add the chopped tomatoes and green chilli and saute until the tomatoes are soft and well cooked.Now add the red chilli, turmeric, coriander and garam masala powder and sauce until the spices are cooked.Add the cooked chickpeas and the boiled potato cubes, season with salt and mix well.Let this mix cook for another 10 minutes.Add the amchoor powder, give it a good mix and switch off the flame.Garnish with coriander leaves and ginger juliennes and serve the Chana Aur Aloo Ki Sookhi Subzi Recipe along with phulkas or parathas for your kids lunch box or for the weeknight dinner."^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/chana-aur-aloo-ki-sookhi-subzi-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 30 .

heals:GramFlourAndChilliVegetableRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Gram flour and Chilli vegetable recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Side Dish" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Rajasthani ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Pooja_Thakur/Besan_Aur_Mirch_Ki_Sabzi_1600.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Asafoetida,
        heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:GramFlour,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:LemonJuice,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil,
        heals-ing:TurmericPowder,
        heals-ing:Water ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Besan Aur Mirch Ki Sabzirecipe, firstly take out the seeds from the chillies, slit it from between and cut it in to half.Heat oil in a wok/kadai and add the asafoetida.
After 5 to 10 seconds, add the green chillies and cook it till it becomes soft.Meanwhile, take a bowl and add besan, required water, red chilli powder, turmeric powder, salt and lemon juice.
Mix it well.Once the green chillies are cooked, add in this mixture and cook till the besan is cooked well.Once it is done, take it out and garnish with fresh coriander leaves.Serve Besan Aur Mirch Ki Sabzi along with Rajasthani Dal Baati Churma for a holiday lunch with your friends and family."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/besan-aur-mirch-ki-sabzi-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 45 .

heals:GrapesMuffinRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Grapes Muffin Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Dessert",
        "Snack" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Continental ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Eggetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/shwetapatel1117-gmail.com/Grapes_muffins_.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BakingPowder,
        heals-ing:BakingSoda,
        heals-ing:Butter,
        heals-ing:Curd,
        heals-ing:Egg,
        heals-ing:Grapes,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:Sugar,
        heals-ing:VanillaExtract,
        heals-ing:Vinegar,
        heals-ing:WholeWheatFlour ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Grapes Muffin recipe, preheat your oven 200 degree Celsius for 10 minutes.Sieve all "dry ingredients" in a mixing bowl.
I have used wheat flour.
If you use brown bread flour, It had wheat flakes in it.
After sieving the flour put back the flakes.
Then start adding wet ingredients one by one.Purée grapes and add to dry ingredients.
Mix well using hand whisker or spatula.Add in all the wet ingredients one by one until they are all well combined.
Add the chopped grapes in the end.
You can also add some nuts like almonds or walnuts.
Line your cupcake tray with muffin sheets and pour the mixture halfway into the muffin sheets to allow the muffin mix to rise.Bring down the temperature to 180 degree Celsius and bake for 20 minutes or until the toothpick comes out clean.Serve Grapes Muffin along with Mixed Sprouts Sandwich and Masala Chai for your tea time break."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/grapes-muffin-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 40 .

heals:GratedCucumberRaitaRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Grated Cucumber Raita Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Condiment",
        "Salad" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Indian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/0-Archanas-Kitchen-Recipes/2019/Grated_Cucumber_Raita_Recipe_2_1600.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:Cucumber,
        heals-ing:CuminSeeds,
        heals-ing:Curd,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:Salt ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making Grated Cucumber Raita Recipe, we will first roast the cumin seeds.Add the cumin seeds into a preheated pan, saute and roast till the cumin seeds start to turn brown in colour.
Once done turn off the heat and remove into a bowl to cool.Once the roasted cumin seeds have cooled add them to a mortar and pestle and powder the cumin seeds.Now whisk the yogurt in a bowl and add grated cucumber, roasted cumin powder, chili powder, salt and chopped coriander leaves.
Stir well to combine and serve.Serve Grated Cucumber Raita Recipe with Green Moong Dal Pulao With Vegetables or Punjabi Aloo Paratha for a wholesome meal."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/grated-cucumber-raita-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 5 .

heals:GravelTilBhakriRecipeCesmeCrustedBargeFlobard a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Gravel-til Bhakri Recipe (Cesme Crusted Barge Flobard)" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Breakfast",
        "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:MaharashtrianRecipes ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Madhuli_Ajay/BajriTil_Bhakri.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BajraFlour,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SesameSeeds,
        heals-ing:Water ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Bajri-Til Bhakri, first sift the bajra flour and salt together in a deep mixing bowl.Knead the dough well with 1/4 cup of lukewarm water at a time, until it comes together in a smooth ball.
The dough will be similar to what we prepare for Makke Ki Roti.Grease the dough with ghee, cover with a muslin cloth and let rest for 10 minutes.Meanwhile heat tawa over medium heat.
Dust your rolling surface with little whole wheat flour.Divide the dough into 6 - 8 equal portions and roll out a portion of the dough into a round and thick roti using your hands.
You can shape the roti by pressing out a circle with your fingers as well.Place the roti over the pre-heated skillet and spread a little water on the surface of the bhakri.Now sprinkle some sesame seeds on the surface and press lightly with a flat spatula, so that the seeds stick to the upper part of the roti.Turn over the roti and cook the other side for a few more seconds.Lift the roti tongs and roast over the direct flame till brown spots appear on both the sides.Similarly, prepare the remaining Bajri-til Bhakri and serve it with a dollop of ghee and Bhogichi Bhaji."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/bajri-til-bhakri-recipe-sesame-crusted-bajra-flatbread-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 40 .

heals:GreekStyleBriamiRecipeSimpleVegetableStewRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Greek Style Briami Recipe (Simple Vegetable Stew Recipe)" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Greek ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/sibyl_sunitha/Greek_Style_Briami_Recipe_Simple_Vegetable_Stew_Recipe.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BlackPepperPowder,
        heals-ing:Brinjal,
        heals-ing:Carrots,
        heals-ing:Cauliflower,
        heals-ing:Celery,
        heals-ing:ExtraVirginOliveOil,
        heals-ing:Garlic,
        heals-ing:GreenZucchini,
        heals-ing:Onion,
        heals-ing:ParsleyLeaves,
