heals:MakhanaAlooTikkiRecipeSpicedLotusSeedPattiesRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Makhana Aloo Tikki Recipe (Spiced Lotus Seed Patties Recipe)" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Snack" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:NorthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/0-Archanas-Kitchen-Recipes/2016/sept-20/Aloo_Paneer_Makhana_Tikki_Recipe_Vrat_Fasting_Food_No_Onion_No_Garlic-2.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BlackSalt,
        heals-ing:ChaatMasalaPowder,
        heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:FennelSeeds,
        heals-ing:GaramMasalaPowder,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:LotusSeeds,
        heals-ing:Potatoes,
        heals-ing:RedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:RoastedPeanuts,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """We begin making the Makhana Aloo Tikki Recipe (Spiced Lotus Seed Patties Recipe) by roasting the makhana in a pan with little bit of ghee until crunchy and coarsely powder it.Mash the potatoes and add all the remaining ingredients in a bowl.
Check the salt and spices and adjust to suit your taste.Shape the aloo makhane mixture into small cutlets and pan fry them in very little oil until golden brown on both sides.Serve your Makhana Aloo Tikki (Spiced Lotus Seed Patties ) with Dhaniya Pudina No Onion No Garlic Chutney to relish your tea time snack."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/makhana-aloo-tikki-recipe-spiced-lotus-seed-patties-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 30 .

heals:MakhaneVegetableRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Makhane vegetable recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:NorthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Madhuri_Aggarwal/Makhana_ki_Sabzi_1600.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BayLeaves,
        heals-ing:Cardamom,
        heals-ing:Cashew,
        heals-ing:CinnamonStick,
        heals-ing:Cloves,
        heals-ing:FreshCream,
        heals-ing:Ghee,
        heals-ing:Ginger,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:GreenPeas,
        heals-ing:Onion,
        heals-ing:PhoolMakhana,
        heals-ing:PoppySeeds,
        heals-ing:PumpkinSeeds,
        heals-ing:RedChilliFlakes,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To start making Makhana ki Sabzi Recipe, get all the ingredients handy.
Pressure cook 2 onions, cashews, magaj and poppy seeds along with enough water.
Blend it into a smooth paste in a mixer grinder and set aside.In a pan heat the ghee and add Makhana to it.
On a medium flame roast the Makhana till they crisp up completely.When you eat them it should be crunchy till the centre and should not be chewy.
Set aside.Heat oil in a pan.
Add bay leaf, cinnamon, cloves, cardamom and sauce it till they give out a nice aroma.Add green chilli and 1 chopped onion and saute till the onion turns light goldAdd fresh green peas and saute for a minute.Add the ground paste, red chilli flakes and saute for a minute.Add 2 cups of water, grated ginger and let it boil for a couple of minutes.Add roasted Makhana to this and let it soak up the liquid and get soft.You will see that the Makhana shrinks in size.
Turn off heat.Serve Makhana ki Sabzi with hot with roti, whole wheat naan, butter naan or phulkas to make a filling lunch or dinner."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/makhana-ki-sabzi-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 40 .

heals:MakkiAndMethiRotiRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Makki and Methi Roti Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Punjabi ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/pooja/Makki_and_Methi_Roti.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:Ajwain,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:KashmiriRedChilliPowder,
        heals-ing:MakkiKaAtta,
        heals-ing:MethiLeaves,
        heals-ing:Salt ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making Makki and Methi Roti Recipe, heat some water in a pan till lukewarm.In a steel mixing bowl, add Maize flour, chopped fenugreek leaves, green chillies, carom seeds and salt.
Mix everything well.
Now add lukewarm water to the maize flour little by little and knead into a soft dough.
Add some oil on top of the entire ball of dough and keep aside.
Place a tawa on low heat and let it heat up.
Next divide the dough into small balls.
Roll out each ball between two sheets of plastic (cling film) into a circle or you can use your hands with the help of wet fingers to make a small round roti.
Place roti on the the tawa and cook it on low flame from both sides until brown spots appear.
Prepare the rest of the the rotis in a similar way and serve hot.
Serve Makki and Methi Roti with Sarson Ka Saag and Burani Raita for a delicious weekday meal."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/makki-and-methi-roti-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 30 .

heals:MakkiKiBakedMathriRecipeBakedCornmealFlakyBiscuit a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Makki Ki Baked Mathri Recipe (Baked Cornmeal Flaky Biscuit)" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Snack" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:NorthIndian ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/Waagmi_Soni/Makki_ki_baked_Mathri.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:CornMeal,
        heals-ing:KasooriMethi,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:SesameSeeds,
        heals-ing:SunflowerOil,
        heals-ing:Water,
        heals-ing:WholeBlackPeppercorns ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making the Makki Ki Baked Mathri recipe, take a bowl and add corn meal (Makki ka aata), salt, crushed black pepper, kasoori methi and oil in the flour.Knead a soft dough with lukewarm water.
Leave the dough covered for 10 to 15 minutes.
Mash the dough to make it soft.Preheat the oven at 180 degree C.
Take out a small lump from the dough and shape it like a ball.
Flatten it a little with both hands.
Now place the Mathris on a baking tray.Bake them for at least 25-30 minutes in an oven or until they turned light brown from both the sides.The delicious Corn flaky Mathris are now ready to serve and eat.
You can put them in an air tight container and you can enjoy them for at least a month.Serve Makki Ki Baked Mathri along with hot masala chai for your tea time break."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/makki-ki-baked-mathri-recipe-baked-cornmeal-flaky-biscuit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 50 .

heals:MalabarKaaiCurryRecipeWithNenthraPazham a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Malabar Kaai Curry Recipe With Nenthra Pazham" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Kerala ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:Vegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/feminasherif-yahoo.com/Kaai_Curry.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BananaFlower,
        heals-ing:Cardamom,
        heals-ing:ChanaDal,
        heals-ing:CoconutMilk,
        heals-ing:Onion,
        heals-ing:Rice,
        heals-ing:Salt,
        heals-ing:Sugar ;
    fkg:hasInstruction "To begin making the Malabar Kaai Curry, first wash and soak chana dal and raw rice separately in two different bowls for about an hour.After that cook chana dal with little salt in water and once done, drain the water and keep it aside.Slice the bananas, and keep them aside.Now, grind together the rice, onion and cardamom with 1 cup water to a very fine paste.Take the rice batter in a pan and to this, add the thin coconut milk.Switch the flame on, and keep stirring continuously till the mixture thickens and becomes creamy.At this stage, add the sugar, salt, cooked chana dal and sliced bananas and mix well.Stir continuously and let the bananas cook for about 10 minutes.After that, add the thick coconut milk and mix and let it boil for about 2 minutes, before switching the flame off.Serve Malabar Kaai Curry as a dessert during the festive season along with Kandarappam."^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/malabar-kaai-curry-recipe-with-nenthrapazham"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 90 .

heals:MalabarMuttonBiryaniRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
    rdfs:label "Malabar Mutton Biryani Recipe" ;
    fkg:hasCourse "Main Course" ;
    fkg:hasCuisine fkg:Malabar ;
    fkg:hasDietType fkg:NonVegetarian ;
    fkg:hasImageURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/images/archanaskitchen/1-Author/garimasgautam-gmail.com/Malabar_Mutton_Biryani.jpg"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:hasIngredient heals-ing:BasmatiRice,
        heals-ing:BayLeaves,
        heals-ing:CardamomPods,
        heals-ing:Cashew,
        heals-ing:CinnamonStick,
        heals-ing:Cloves,
        heals-ing:CorianderLeaves,
        heals-ing:CorianderPowder,
        heals-ing:CuminSeeds,
        heals-ing:Curd,
        heals-ing:FennelSeeds,
        heals-ing:Ghee,
        heals-ing:GingerGarlicPaste,
        heals-ing:GreenChilli,
        heals-ing:Milk,
        heals-ing:MintLeaves,
        heals-ing:Mutton,
        heals-ing:Onion,
        heals-ing:Raisins,
        heals-ing:Saffron,
        heals-ing:Tomatoes,
        heals-ing:Water,
        heals-ing:WholeBlackPeppercorns ;
    fkg:hasInstruction """To begin making Malabar Mutton Biryani Recipe, prep all the ingredients well.
Once done, take the ingredients for biryani masala in a mixer grinder and grind to a smooth paste with the help of little water.
Also soak basmati rice in water for 10-15 minutes.Heat the ghee in a cast iron or heavy bottomed kadai; Once the ghee is hot but not yet smoking, add the sliced onions and saute till golden brown in colour and caramelized.
You can take these onions out and add them at the end of the recipe for a nice texture.Now into the same pan, add the sliced tomatoes and saute well till mushy.Once the tomatoes are mushy, add in ginger garlic paste, curd and freshly ground biryani masala paste, cardamom, turmeric powder, and coriander powder and saute a bit till the raw smell of ginger garlic paste goes away.
Add the mutton pieces and cook well with lid closed.Melt the ghee in a biryani pot and add in the remaining spices- green chillies, mint, coriander leaves, cashew nuts, raisins, bay leaves and saute till brown in colour.Add milk, curd, and water.
Wait till it comes to a boil and then add rice.
Add salt to taste.
Lower the heat, cover the pan with a lid and continue to cook for 15 minutes or till teh rice is done.Take another biryani pot, place half the rice into it.
Now layer the cooked flavourful mutton on the top of the rice.
Add the remaining rice on top of the mutton.
Spread the contents of the pan to make an even layer.
Make random holes through the rice with a spoon and pour into each a little saffron milk.Place a few spoons of ghee, caramelized onion, cashew nuts and raisins on the surface and cover tightly.
Serve the biryani hot.Serve Malabar Mutton Biryani Recipe along with Biriyani Chammanthi Recipe (Green Chutney Recipe) and Masala Chaas Recipe (Indian Spiced Buttermilk)."""^^xsd:string ;
    fkg:hasURL "https://www.archanaskitchen.com/malabar-mutton-biryani-recipe"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    fkg:preparationTime 60 .

heals:MalabarStyleDatesCorianderChutneyRecipe a heals:Recipe ;
